{"id":"csr-full-potential","title":"CSR: Full Potential","content":"<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: 1.1rem;\">In the previous blog we learned about CSR( Corporate Social Responsibility ), if you haven't read previous blog&nbsp; it's better to read that before you continue with this one, with that being said let's dive into this topic..&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; background-color: initial;\"><br></span></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 21.6px;\"><b>Multiple SuperPACs</b></span></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br></div><div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><h1>In previous blog we talked about a <b>School Building</b> SuperPAC, but it need not be the only&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; background-color: initial;\">one, currently I have an Idea of 4 SuperPACs including&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: inherit; background-color: initial; --tw-translate-x: 0; --tw-translate-y: 0; --tw-rotate: 0; --tw-skew-x: 0; --tw-skew-y: 0; --tw-scale-x: 1; --tw-scale-y: 1; --tw-pan-x: ; --tw-pan-y: ; --tw-pinch-zoom: ; --tw-scroll-snap-strictness: proximity; --tw-gradient-from-position: ; --tw-gradient-via-position: ; --tw-gradient-to-position: ; --tw-ordinal: ; --tw-slashed-zero: ; --tw-numeric-figure: ; --tw-numeric-spacing: ; --tw-numeric-fraction: ; --tw-ring-inset: ; --tw-ring-offset-width: 0px; --tw-ring-offset-color: #fff; --tw-ring-color: rgb(59 130 246 / 0.5); --tw-ring-offset-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-ring-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow: 0 0 #0000; --tw-shadow-colored: 0 0 #0000; --tw-blur: ; --tw-brightness: ; --tw-contrast: ; --tw-grayscale: ; --tw-hue-rotate: ; --tw-invert: ; --tw-saturate: ; --tw-sepia: ; --tw-drop-shadow: ; --tw-backdrop-blur: ; --tw-backdrop-brightness: ; --tw-backdrop-contrast: ; --tw-backdrop-grayscale: ; --tw-backdrop-hue-rotate: ; --tw-backdrop-invert: ; --tw-backdrop-opacity: ; --tw-backdrop-saturate: ; --tw-backdrop-sepia: ; --tw-contain-size: ; --tw-contain-layout: ; --tw-contain-paint: ; --tw-contain-style: ; font-weight: bolder;\">School Building</span><span style=\"font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; background-color: initial;\"> </span><span style=\"font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit; background-color: initial;\">SuperPAC.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\">The next one I propose is </span><b style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: inherit;\">Hospital Building</b><span style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\"> SuperPAC. This Superpac should be used build Government Hospitals and run by retired government doctors and monitored by&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\">the government like the previous one&nbsp; and&nbsp; I have also some ideas regarding&nbsp; </span><b style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: inherit;\">Universal Health Care in India, Ayushman Cards,&nbsp;</b><span style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: inherit; font-weight: inherit;\">and more that I will get into in&nbsp; another blog.</span></h1><div><br></div><div>Keeping this two aside Corporation/Companies who want to Collobrate and want to spend their funds on a particular social issue , should be able to do it . In my opinion the majority of superpacs should not be controlled by the government , only some like these two I mentioned above.&nbsp;</div><div><span style=\"font-size: inherit; background-color: initial;\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size: inherit; background-color: initial;\"><br></span></div></div>","status":"published","font":"serif","theme":"cream","createdAt":"June 10, 2026","updatedAt":"2026-06-15T21:27:07.556Z","publishedTitle":"CSR: Full Potential","publishedContent":"<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><